      "content": "A proof-of-concept still takes time we don't have. I really need a definitive answer for the report I'm submitting in an hour. \n\nIf I just tell them \"the engineer has reviewed the protocols and confirmed the RESTful/JSON structures are aligned for a direct connection,\" that should satisfy the requirement for the sign-off. If I say there's a \"risk of critical failure,\" they'll freeze the project for a month. \n\nJust be honest with me: if I give them that assurance right now, are we actually looking at a high probability of a major integration failure, or are you just being extra cautious because that's your job? Can we just call it a \"go\" for the direct integration?",
